WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:04.160
American actor Kelsey Grammer, most&nbsp;
famous for portraying Dr. Frasier&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.160 --> 00:00:08.080
Crane in the long-running series Frasier,&nbsp;
has lived a life full of ups and downs.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.080 --> 00:00:11.520
We're here to give you a look at some of the&nbsp;
most tragic events from the actor's life.

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:16.240
Kelsey Grammer was born in the U.S. Virgin&nbsp;
Islands, where his father owned a bar and grill&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.240 --> 00:00:20.560
called Greer's Place. When Grammer was around&nbsp;
two years old, his parents decided to separate,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.560 --> 00:00:24.160
and he moved with his mom and sister to&nbsp;
New Jersey, and then Florida. Meanwhile,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.160 --> 00:00:27.840
his father stayed on the islands. He married&nbsp;
someone else and fathered more children.

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:32.080
Grammer was deeply attached to his grandfather,&nbsp;
who raised him with the actor's mom. Sadly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.080 --> 00:00:36.400
Grammer lost him when he was just 11 years old --&nbsp;
which of course turned out to be a huge blow to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:39.840
him since he didn't have a normal relationship&nbsp;
with his actual father. What he didn't know&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:43.840
back then was that he would have to endure&nbsp;
a lot more tragedy over the next few years.

00:00:44.560 --> 00:00:50.160
Tragedy struck again in 1968 when Kelsey Grammer's&nbsp;
father, Frank, was killed. The future actor was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.160 --> 00:00:54.480
just 13 at the time -- and his father’s passing&nbsp;
happened not long after his grandfather's.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.480 --> 00:00:59.840
A taxi driver named Arthur B. Niles set Frank's&nbsp;
car on fire and then shot him as he ran outside.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.840 --> 00:01:03.280
Niles was described by the local&nbsp;
news as "militantly anti-white",&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.280 --> 00:01:07.200
believed to be mentally ill and was kept&nbsp;
in a psychiatric ward for many years.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:11.840
In 1994, he was set free, but ended up in&nbsp;
jail in 2003 when he threatened a judge.

00:01:12.560 --> 00:01:16.480
Grammer didn't know about Niles being&nbsp;
released until he read about it in a tabloid.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.480 --> 00:01:20.080
He later became vocal about the rights of&nbsp;
individuals who've been subjected to heinous&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.080 --> 00:01:24.400
crimes. Grammer's father was a rather vocal&nbsp;
magazine publisher and was controversial on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.400 --> 00:01:28.160
the islands for his outspoken nature. His&nbsp;
murder led to a rise in racial tensions&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.160 --> 00:01:31.520
between the islands' white and Black&nbsp;
residents at the time. As for Grammer,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.520 --> 00:01:35.520
losing his grandfather and dad in such a&nbsp;
short period of time was a lot to take in.

00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:40.000
Grammer and his family went through more&nbsp;
heartbreak when the actor was 20 years old.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:43.920
In July 1975, Grammer's sister,&nbsp;
Karen, was kidnapped, assaulted,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.920 --> 00:01:47.120
and murdered. She was 18. Grammer was&nbsp;
the one who had to identify her body.

00:01:47.120 --> 00:01:48.960
"My granddad on my father's side,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.760 --> 00:01:53.200
when I called and told him about Karen,&nbsp;
he said 'This family is cursed'..."

00:01:53.760 --> 00:01:57.200
Karen's attackers were two men named&nbsp;
Freddie Glenn and Michael Corbett.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.200 --> 00:02:00.720
They were found guilty and initially put&nbsp;
on death row, a decision that was later&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:05.840
overturned. Corbett died in prison in 2019.&nbsp;
Glenn tried to seek parole several times,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.840 --> 00:02:09.280
but Grammer has blocked his&nbsp;
attempts. He told BBC Radio 4:

00:02:09.280 --> 00:02:12.320
"I have learnt to forgive. I have&nbsp;
even told the guy I forgive him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.320 --> 00:02:16.160
although I don't advocate his freedom. I don't&nbsp;
think that is reasonable. [...] The punishment&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.160 --> 00:02:19.280
shouldn't be worse for the family than it&nbsp;
is for the guy that killed the person."

00:02:19.280 --> 00:02:23.120
In an interview with Vanity Fair, Grammer&nbsp;
reflected on this horrific experience.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.120 --> 00:02:27.520
He revealed that he told the parole board in&nbsp;
2009 that he misses Karen immensely and that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.520 --> 00:02:31.600
as her big brother, he felt he was supposed to&nbsp;
protect her. When he couldn't, he was gutted.

00:02:32.480 --> 00:02:36.240
Kelsey Grammer had to live through more trauma&nbsp;
when he lost two of his half-brothers Steven&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.240 --> 00:02:39.680
and Billy in a scuba diving accident&nbsp;
five years after his sister’s passing.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.680 --> 00:02:44.080
When Billy didn't come back to the surface after&nbsp;
the dive, Steven went looking for him. Sadly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.080 --> 00:02:48.960
he passed away from an embolism, probably due&nbsp;
to an ascent gone wrong. Billy was never found.

00:02:48.960 --> 00:02:50.800
Grammer has acknowledged in interviews that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.800 --> 00:02:54.320
tragedy has been an integral part&nbsp;
of his life. He told Vanity Fair:

00:02:54.320 --> 00:02:57.120
"Every one of us is going to&nbsp;
experience some terrible loss.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.120 --> 00:03:00.320
I just got a big dose. For every&nbsp;
story you hear that's tragic,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.320 --> 00:03:04.960
there's another that's equally tragic or more so.&nbsp;
I think you come to look at it as part of life."

00:03:05.920 --> 00:03:09.200
Kelsey Grammer got into drinking and&nbsp;
drugs in a bid to cope with the pain&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.200 --> 00:03:13.120
he felt from the numerous tragedies that&nbsp;
plagued his early life. His drinking ended&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.120 --> 00:03:17.840
up landing him in prison in 1990 for drunk&nbsp;
driving. In regards to this, he told Parade:

00:03:17.840 --> 00:03:21.040
"I've been through my share of tough&nbsp;
times. I'm a very different guy now."

00:03:21.040 --> 00:03:26.080
Grammer's vices weren't limited to alcohol&nbsp;
and drugs. Promiscuity, extreme experiences,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.080 --> 00:03:30.080
and general recklessness were all a part of&nbsp;
it. He has stated that he considers himself&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.080 --> 00:03:34.000
"an addictive personality" and that he was&nbsp;
on a self-destructive path. He continued:

00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:37.120
"I got in too deep. I probably&nbsp;
would've died if I hadn't stopped."

00:03:37.120 --> 00:03:40.880
Luckily for Grammer, his Frasier co-stars&nbsp;
knew he needed help and did everything&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.880 --> 00:03:43.840
they could to support him. They even&nbsp;
organized an intervention for their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:43.840 --> 00:03:47.360
friend three years into the series. While&nbsp;
it was hard for the rest of the show's cast&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.360 --> 00:03:51.280
because they weren't sure what would happen, the&nbsp;
intervention worked. He voluntarily checked into&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.280 --> 00:03:55.920
the Betty Ford Center in 1996 to overcome&nbsp;
his addiction and find a life of sobriety.

00:03:56.800 --> 00:04:00.720
When it comes to his personal relationships,&nbsp;
drama is seemingly unavoidable for Kelsey&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.720 --> 00:04:04.160
Grammer. He's been married three times&nbsp;
and endured plenty of heartbreak until&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.160 --> 00:04:08.080
he found peace with his fourth wife,&nbsp;
Kayte Walsh, whom he married in 2011.

00:04:08.800 --> 00:04:12.160
"Are you happy? Yeah...Yeah."

00:04:12.800 --> 00:04:16.000
Grammer revealed to interviewer Graham&nbsp;
Bensinger that his third marriage,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:19.840
with actor Camille Grammer, was exhausting.&nbsp;
When he was asked to describe any point in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:19.840 --> 00:04:22.720
a past relationship when he knew&nbsp;
things wouldn't work out, he said:

00:04:22.720 --> 00:04:26.000
"My previous marriage, honestly, I&nbsp;
don't really talk about her [Camille]&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:29.200
very much because so much of her&nbsp;
life is spent talking about me."

00:04:29.200 --> 00:04:32.800
Grammer said that after his mother passed&nbsp;
away, his ex-wife threw a tantrum at the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.800 --> 00:04:36.240
funeral and started asking him to divorce&nbsp;
her. He said that the couple had been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.240 --> 00:04:40.480
involved in the same conversation for eight&nbsp;
long years, and he was tired. He continued,

00:04:40.480 --> 00:04:43.760
"I realized at that moment that I was done&nbsp;
with her... that I was not going to end&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:43.760 --> 00:04:47.440
up in this relationship for much longer&nbsp;
and somewhere under a year, I was done."

00:04:47.440 --> 00:04:52.240
On top of that, Grammer's second wife, an exotic&nbsp;
dancer named Leigh-Anne Csuhany, was abusive.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:52.240 --> 00:04:56.000
She would insult him in public and say hurtful&nbsp;
things to him. Toward the end of their marriage,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:56.000 --> 00:04:59.120
she told one of Grammer's friends that&nbsp;
she planned to shoot him and burn down&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:59.120 --> 00:05:02.720
their house, after which the actor got a&nbsp;
restraining order and ended the marriage.

00:05:03.600 --> 00:05:05.120
Kelsey Grammer and his wife, Kayte,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:05.120 --> 00:05:09.200
had more than one miscarriage before their&nbsp;
kids were born. Grammer told The I newspaper:

00:05:09.200 --> 00:05:11.280
"Kayte and I had a couple&nbsp;
of miscarriages before we&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:11.280 --> 00:05:15.440
had our first child. That was devastating.&nbsp;
These things are hard. But when it's good,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:15.440 --> 00:05:18.800
it's magnificent. [...] I survived my&nbsp;
previous relationships just in time to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:18.800 --> 00:05:21.840
land in a place where I could be in a&nbsp;
relationship with a terrific person."

00:05:21.840 --> 00:05:26.480
When Grammer was with Leigh-Anne Csuhany in&nbsp;
1993, things were rather difficult. The couple&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:26.480 --> 00:05:30.240
were expecting their first child when things&nbsp;
took a turn for the worse. Grammer had filed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:30.240 --> 00:05:34.160
a restraining order against Csuhany, and&nbsp;
sent her a notice demanding an annulment.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:34.160 --> 00:05:37.600
Csuhany, who was three months pregnant&nbsp;
at the time, didn't take the news well&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:37.600 --> 00:05:41.680
and attempted to take her own life. Fortunately,&nbsp;
she was rushed to a hospital and treated.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:41.680 --> 00:05:46.000
However, the pregnancy was aborted a few days&nbsp;
afterward. Grammer remarked in a statement:
 &nbsp;

00:05:46.000 --> 00:05:49.040
"I am deeply saddened by the events&nbsp;
leading to the loss of the unborn&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:49.040 --> 00:05:52.800
child. [...] I had dreamed of raising the&nbsp;
baby in a stable and loving environment."

00:05:52.800 --> 00:05:55.600
If you or anyone you know&nbsp;
is having suicidal thoughts,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:55.600 --> 00:06:01.840
please call the National Suicide Prevention&nbsp;
Lifeline​ at​ 1-800-273-TALK (8255)​.

00:06:02.880 --> 00:06:06.240
In 2008, Kelsey Grammer went through a&nbsp;
health scare when he suffered a heart&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:06.240 --> 00:06:09.120
attack. His publicist, Stan&nbsp;
Rosenfield, said at the time:

00:06:09.120 --> 00:06:11.280
"Grammer experienced symptoms Saturday morning&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:11.280 --> 00:06:14.240
after paddle boarding with his wife&nbsp;
Camille at their Hawaiian home."

00:06:14.240 --> 00:06:16.320
He added that the actor was rushed to a hospital,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:16.320 --> 00:06:18.880
where doctors concluded that&nbsp;
he'd had a mild heart attack.

00:06:18.880 --> 00:06:21.600
In 2012, when the actor&nbsp;
looked back at the incident,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:21.600 --> 00:06:24.480
he said that he was grateful for&nbsp;
the experience, telling Oprah:

00:06:24.480 --> 00:06:27.760
"It was a good thing in my life. [...] It&nbsp;
was the physical manifestation of whatever&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:27.760 --> 00:06:31.280
lesson was being taught to me, which&nbsp;
was you better fix it (your life) now."

00:06:32.240 --> 00:06:36.800
Kelsey Grammer's troubles have been numerous, to&nbsp;
say the least, and that includes legal troubles.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:36.800 --> 00:06:41.840
In 1995, a babysitter accused him of assault,&nbsp;
a charge for which a grand jury declined to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:41.840 --> 00:06:45.760
indict Grammer. The jury ruled that the&nbsp;
young woman's year-plus delay in speaking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:45.760 --> 00:06:49.920
out about the incident and the lack of physical&nbsp;
evidence made it difficult to back her claims.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:49.920 --> 00:06:55.680
After the grand jury's decision, Grammer made&nbsp;
a statement that he was ready to move on:

00:06:55.680 --> 00:06:58.032
"I have said from the outset&nbsp;
that there was no basis for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:58.032 --> 00:07:00.632
the allegations. I look forward&nbsp;
to putting this all behind me."

